<title>BRAZIL: Brazil central bank chief to step down - minister.</title>
<headline>Brazil central bank chief to step down - minister.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian Central Bank President Gustavo Loyola will step down and International Affairs Director Gustavo Franco has been nominated to replace him, a top government official said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Gustavo Loyola is leaving the presidency of the Central Bank,&quot; Finance Minister Pedro Malan told reporters. Malan said Franco had been nominated to replace Loyola. His nomination faced confirmation by the Senate.</p>
<p>Malan said Loyola had completed his stated task of ensuring the reconstruction of the Brazilian banking sector.</p>
<p>Both were giving a news conference.</p>
<p>((--Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom, 5561 3141193)</p>
